					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doorhandle" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5532328); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5532328&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795075" alt="Doorhandle" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5532328)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doorhandle" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5532328); return false;" >Doorhandle</a></span> <span class="odate time_1585485753 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Mar 2020 12:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4570595">
									

<p>Hello, good sir! Congratulations on your first SCP! I was quite delighted to be able to give a critique to this beforehand, and your end result seems to be even better than the last time I checked it.</p>
<p>For real though, I really enjoyed the last interview with SCP-5151, since you gave some fragments of its personality early on, with that final bit showing that it might actually have some remorse for its actions. Good stuff.</p>
<p>To be honest, I was only a bit bothered by some minor SPAG mistakes, though I do have some improvements for that. Do keep in mind that this is coming from someone who really craves line-by-line perfection, so please forgive this manic man for his bad habit.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Line-by-line-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;by-line-by-line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>All right, <span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><span style="color: red">red and crossed out</span></span> = deleted; <span style="color: blue">blue</span> = replacement.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>MTF Epsilon-11 Commander's message</strong></p>
<p>SCP-4878 has been returned to Site-119 and <span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><span style="color: red">has been</span></span> placed under enhanced security.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Addendum 5151.07: Incident Report 5151.IR.01</strong></p>
<p>Pi-7-1 proceeded to fire a taser at SCP-5151<span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><span style="color: red">. After being hit by the taser, SCP-5151</span></span> <span style="color: blue">causing it to</span> convulse<span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><span style="color: red">d</span></span> for a brief moment&#8230;[ ]</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>O5 Response</strong></p>
<p>[ ]&#8230;Security Director Oliver Albury has been administered a Class C amnestic and <span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><span style="color: red">has been</span></span> demoted to D-class.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Gerard Hansjörg's message</strong></p>
<p>Dr. Richter, <span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><span style="color: red">Y</span></span><span style="color: blue">y</span>our input and concerns have been noted,&#8230;[ ]</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Other than that, most of the stuff here is pretty good! Really glad to see that you managed to make an unkillable humanoid that's still interesting!</p>
<p>Also, you might need to announce your SCP in <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-13092342/scp-announcements-44:there-is-something-at-work-in-my-soul">this forum</a> so that it can gain some needed traction.</p>
<p>Good luck to you and a good day (or night) to all who are reading this!</p>

							</div>

