					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nzsaltz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5092913); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5092913&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795075" alt="nzsaltz" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5092913)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nzsaltz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5092913); return false;" >nzsaltz</a></span> <span class="odate time_1585525954 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Mar 2020 23:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4571041">
									

<p>This was great when I read the draft, and it's even better now. Great 1st SCP. I would say that some of the doctors felt a bit stilted in the interview logs, but that could just be intentional for how they would talk to a scip. I have some very specific line-by-line stuff, but other than that, I like the story and progression.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Line-by-line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Sorry&nbsp;for&nbsp;being&nbsp;so&nbsp;picky</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Consult the on-Site culinary team for further details on SCP-5151's &quot;banquet&quot; requests.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This line is fine, but the footnote is in the wrong place. It should be after the next sentence, when it talks about the banquets.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Despite the appearance of having clothing and armor, every aspect of SCP-5151's body, garments, armor, longsword, and other adornments are all made up of the same composition.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Technically, since aspect is singular and the list is a preposition referring to aspect, it should read &quot;every aspect&#8230; is made up of the same composition&quot; instead of &quot;every aspect&#8230; are all made up of the same composition.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5151 has an anomalous ability to judge a person's character and decide whether or not they are honorable.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's not an anomalous ability in itself. You should include something like &quot;instantly&quot; and/or &quot;upon observing them,&quot; which is the actual anomalous ability. I can decide whether or not you are honorable (I'll say you are), but I'm not anomalous.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Current research is being conducted on the nature of SCP-5151 and the nature and removal of SCP-5151-2.</span> Current research is being conducted on possible containment and restraint procedures for SCP-5151 by unconventional means, as well as the nature and removal of SCP-5151-2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You basically just said the same thing twice. Unless a perfect containment method is found for an object, or if it's Safe class, then any research will be, at least partially, to find means of containment. Just take out one of them and it's fine.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>MTF Pi-1 ceased their fire, and SCP-5151 proceeded to greet them with &quot;<em>Brave fellows</em>,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Honestly, I'm not sure if this is fully incorrect, but it sounds awkward. Take out the &quot;with&quot; and put a comma after &quot;them.&quot; (It should read, &quot;proceeded to greet them, '<em>Brave fellows</em>,'&quot;)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I would like to interview you, but would you first explain your reasoning for why you killed one of our agents despite sparing the remaining agents who were attacking you?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The word &quot;but&quot; implies a contrasting statement. For instance, if you said, &quot;I wanted ice cream, but it was too cold,&quot; those two statements contrast. Those two statements in the article do not contrast, so I would say to just replace &quot;but&quot; with a period. (It should say, &quot;interview you. Would you&quot;)</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>I swear I am the only one who hasn't lost their head over this new mark.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Put a comma after &quot;swear.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the future, harsher penalties will be administered if the Foundation ever witnesses a breach of security along the lines of an event of this scale.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't see any reason for &quot;along the lines of an event.&quot; Just take that out so it says, &quot;a breach of security of this scale.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr. Richter:</strong> But something still seems to bother you, doesn't it, 5151?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would he be able to tell that? Dr. Richter was just assigned to this scip. Maybe move the <em>(visibly bothered)</em> to before that line, or put something like that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What do you have to say regarding this new information, 5151?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I see no reason for this line to exist. He asks if he has input after that, anyways, and so, to me, it just sounds really stilted. I say take it out.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I have concluded that SCP-5151's hidden identity belongs to Honos</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Hidden identity&quot;? Unless I'm mistaken, nothing before in the article suggested that the researchers thought he had a &quot;hidden identity.&quot; It was revealed that he had gone by different names, but it was very unclear. It's not a big deal, but I would say replace &quot;hidden identity&quot; with &quot;true identity.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On a side-note, Site Director, my research team is currently terrified.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I know this is supposed to sound scary and threatening, and all that, but it really just comes off as funny to me. Just offhandedly telling your superior, &quot;By the way, we're scared out of our minds,&quot; is just weirdly funny to me. I don't really know how you should change it, though.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Concerning SCP-500, that will be something that I will need to discuss with others.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This line feels kind of stilted. I think it's the &quot;with others&quot; tacked on at the end. I would suggest changing it to passive voice and just saying, &quot;that will need to be discussed later in the future.&quot;</p>
<p>Either way, it's not a conclusive final line at all. Not saying that it needs to be, but especially for heavily narrative based articles, it just doesn't feel very climactic. Take the ending of SCP-5002, for example: &quot;Reader, I very much hope that you feel the same way. About me, and about yourself.&quot; That hits hard. That's just a suggestion, though, not necessary at all.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyways, +1.</p>

							</div>

								
					
