			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4581928">
									

<p>As I mentioned in IRC, this suffers from two main issues that kept me from upvoting it.</p>
<p>First, it's too damn long for the rather basic and predictable story that you're telling. I figured out that the blood pact was going to go sour literally as soon as the researchers made it. Your conprocs sell the reveal way too early, and then you put thousands of words between when a reader figures out your reveal and when it actually pays off.</p>
<p>The second, and much harder to fix, issue is that your version of the Foundation is being mind-numbingly dumb here. They cater to every desire of the SCP and give it all of the power when they have no reason to. They could have sealed the containment chamber immediately right at the start of the article and been done with it. He could have even been a Safe or Euclid anomaly if they just shoved him in a box and left him there. The incompetence of the Foundation drew me out of your plot before it had even gotten started and it helped further to telegraph your ending too early.</p>
<p>This is a -1 from me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
